{
  "iri": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_2043",
  "lang": "en",
  "description": [
    "A viral hepatitis that results_in inflammation located_in liver, has_material_basis_in Hepatitis B virus (Orthohepadnavirus hominoidei), which is transmitted_by sexual contact, blood transfusions, or fomites like needles or syringes. The infection has_symptom fever, fatigue, loss of appetite, nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, clay-colored bowel movements, joint pain, and jaundice."
  ],
  "synonyms": [
    "Serum hepatitis",
